WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.583
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.616 --> 00:00:15.857
- Hi, I'm Hannah, your
friendly neighborhood wine mom,

00:00:15.857 --> 00:00:16.924
and if you're anything like me

00:00:16.924 --> 00:00:18.743
you believe that a glass
of wine at 8:00 p.m.

00:00:18.743 --> 00:00:19.877
makes you a better mom,

00:00:19.877 --> 00:00:21.753
so pour yourself a glass and let's talk.

00:00:21.753 --> 00:00:22.711
It's fall, y'all.

00:00:22.711 --> 00:00:24.628
In celebration of that,

00:00:25.612 --> 00:00:27.996
I found pumpkin spice wine.

00:00:27.996 --> 00:00:29.701
I didn't know that it was possible

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:33.133
for me to be any more basic
but dreams do come true.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.587
So we're going to celebrate
with a glass of that.

00:00:35.587 --> 00:00:36.574
It's not flavored.

00:00:36.574 --> 00:00:39.282
It's literal pumpkin wine,

00:00:39.282 --> 00:00:41.520
which I thought only
existed in Harry Potter,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.123
which is why I'm wearing this sorting hat.

00:00:43.123 --> 00:00:43.956
Cheers.

00:00:45.976 --> 00:00:46.980
Ugh!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.749
Oh my God, this is so gross!

00:00:48.749 --> 00:00:49.582
(Hannah wines)

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.355
I was so excited.

00:00:51.355 --> 00:00:52.335
I gotta get something else.

00:00:52.335 --> 00:00:53.168
(camera beeps)

00:00:53.168 --> 00:00:54.137
Okay.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:54.970
Let's try this again.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.838
I got some real mom wine, chardonnay.

00:00:57.838 --> 00:01:00.694
So with fall comes my
favorite holiday, Halloween.

00:01:00.694 --> 00:01:03.072
I love it because I love candy.

00:01:03.072 --> 00:01:05.046
And even though I love Halloween,

00:01:05.046 --> 00:01:06.491
not all good things are perfect,

00:01:06.491 --> 00:01:09.809
so let's talk about the
worst parts about Halloween.

00:01:09.809 --> 00:01:11.966
First, the kids' costume situation.

00:01:11.966 --> 00:01:14.438
Every year, starting in April,

00:01:14.438 --> 00:01:16.890
my son decides what he
wants to be for Halloween,

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.719
so I'll always get conned
into buying that costume.

00:01:19.719 --> 00:01:21.423
And the next week he changes his mind.

00:01:21.423 --> 00:01:24.633
My rule is if he doesn't
change his mind for a month

00:01:24.633 --> 00:01:25.752
I will buy the costume.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.061
He's dead set on being Kylo Ren this year.

00:01:28.061 --> 00:01:30.506
So we got the costume,
I go to the checkout.

00:01:30.506 --> 00:01:31.598
50 dollars.

00:01:31.598 --> 00:01:32.902
50 dollars!

00:01:32.902 --> 00:01:34.941
And I'm like, okay, this is worth it.

00:01:34.941 --> 00:01:37.033
It's in all the Star Wars packaging.

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:39.848
And this probably has, like,
laser beams flying out of it

00:01:39.848 --> 00:01:41.062
if it's 50 dollars.

00:01:41.062 --> 00:01:42.333
50 dollars!

00:01:42.333 --> 00:01:45.875
And we unwrap it and it's
literally one piece of fabric

00:01:45.875 --> 00:01:48.805
with some slits on it,
and then a plastic mask.

00:01:48.805 --> 00:01:50.205
50 dollars!

00:01:50.205 --> 00:01:52.388
To be worn one day of the year.

00:01:52.388 --> 00:01:54.812
And as a mom, that's, like, offensive.

00:01:54.812 --> 00:01:58.645
I need everything to be worn
to its maximum capacity.

00:01:58.645 --> 00:02:01.645
So if I'm spending 50 dollars
on a Kylo Ren costume,

00:02:01.645 --> 00:02:02.849
50 dollars,

00:02:02.849 --> 00:02:04.281
he's gonna wear it to school,

00:02:04.281 --> 00:02:05.366
he's gonna wear it to the park,

00:02:05.366 --> 00:02:06.829
he's gonna wear it to restaurants,

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:08.868
he's gonna wear it to gymnastics class.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:10.199
"You keep that mask on!

00:02:10.199 --> 00:02:11.676
"I don't care if you can't see.

00:02:11.676 --> 00:02:14.633
"Tumble with the mask on, we're
getting our money's worth."

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:17.527
Next, the mom costume situation.

00:02:17.527 --> 00:02:18.360
Because apparently,

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.009
if you're shopping at a
costume store as a mother,

00:02:21.009 --> 00:02:24.859
you either can have no body
or show your entire body.

00:02:24.859 --> 00:02:25.692
As a mother,

00:02:25.692 --> 00:02:28.111
I feel like when I'm going
trick-or-treating with my kids,

00:02:28.111 --> 00:02:31.101
there's an expectation of
me to have a modest costume,

00:02:31.101 --> 00:02:34.506
but I don't wanna be a
freakin' crayon for Halloween.

00:02:34.506 --> 00:02:37.319
I wish there was some type
of middle ground costume

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:38.152
that I could buy.

00:02:38.152 --> 00:02:39.940
Cat Woman meets Cat Lady.

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.475
Like Cat Woman, but not skintight.

00:02:42.475 --> 00:02:44.211
Like, give me a little room to breathe.

00:02:44.211 --> 00:02:47.729
Maybe after she's retired
and had a couple of kids.

00:02:47.729 --> 00:02:49.600
That's the costume that I want.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.773
If you're looking to start a business,

00:02:51.773 --> 00:02:54.170
moderately sexy costumes for moms.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.807
You're welcome.

00:02:55.807 --> 00:02:57.375
Next, the crash.

00:02:57.375 --> 00:03:00.658
So throughout trick-or-treating
my child will ask

00:03:00.658 --> 00:03:03.794
for a piece of candy from
each house that we visit

00:03:03.794 --> 00:03:04.627
and he'll be like,

00:03:04.627 --> 00:03:06.264
"Oh my God, but Mom,
they gave me a Kit Kat!"

00:03:06.264 --> 00:03:07.966
Like you don't know what a Kit Kat is.

00:03:07.966 --> 00:03:09.718
You know how to con me better than that.

00:03:09.718 --> 00:03:10.659
Come on.

00:03:10.659 --> 00:03:13.222
He ends up eating pieces
of candy all along the way.

00:03:13.222 --> 00:03:14.494
By the we get home,

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:17.170
both of my children are
just puddles of mush.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.957
Only 90s kids will remember
the Capri Sun commercials

00:03:19.957 --> 00:03:23.177
where, like, the kids turn
into these gelatinous, like,

00:03:23.177 --> 00:03:26.158
silver things and, like,
melted into the ground.

00:03:26.158 --> 00:03:27.944
Like, that's what my children turn into.

00:03:27.944 --> 00:03:29.314
Then you have to brush their teeth

00:03:29.314 --> 00:03:30.633
and they never want to brush their teeth

00:03:30.633 --> 00:03:33.632
and it's like, "Dude, you
just ingested 80 cavities."

00:03:33.632 --> 00:03:34.465
By the end of the night

00:03:34.465 --> 00:03:36.685
it's like I've just
fought in the Crusades.

00:03:36.685 --> 00:03:39.290
But it's all worth it because
once they fall asleep,

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.790
that candy's mine.

00:03:41.816 --> 00:03:42.649
Okay.

00:03:42.649 --> 00:03:44.078
The hat's coming off.

00:03:44.078 --> 00:03:45.495
Feel like I should look in the mirror.

00:03:45.495 --> 00:03:47.364
Last, Neil Patrick Harris.

00:03:47.364 --> 00:03:48.409
We all know him.

00:03:48.409 --> 00:03:49.327
We all love him.

00:03:49.327 --> 00:03:50.845
He is perfect.

00:03:50.845 --> 00:03:52.515
His husband is perfect.

00:03:52.515 --> 00:03:54.293
Their children are perfect.

00:03:54.293 --> 00:03:57.355
And instead of just, like,
privately enjoying it

00:03:57.355 --> 00:03:59.586
every year they post

00:03:59.586 --> 00:04:03.455
the most perfect
Halloween costume ensemble

00:04:03.455 --> 00:04:06.322
that I have every seen in
my stupid, worthless life.

00:04:06.322 --> 00:04:09.563
They always the most perfectly
coordinated costumes, too,

00:04:09.563 --> 00:04:11.227
and it's always something popular

00:04:11.227 --> 00:04:12.888
but not overdone that year.

00:04:12.888 --> 00:04:14.526
Well how do they know
that they're going to be

00:04:14.526 --> 00:04:18.058
the only family dressed as
perfect Peter Pan characters?

00:04:18.058 --> 00:04:19.638
You have Halloween all to yourself.

00:04:19.638 --> 00:04:20.715
You are the only people

00:04:20.715 --> 00:04:22.656
who are worthy of
celebrating this holiday.

00:04:22.656 --> 00:04:24.802
When my family tries
to coordinate costumes,

00:04:24.802 --> 00:04:26.910
we look like a bunch of crazy people

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:27.828
walking down the street.

00:04:27.828 --> 00:04:30.839
And they always take
this perfect family photo

00:04:30.839 --> 00:04:31.884
in their costumes.

00:04:31.884 --> 00:04:34.772
Everyone is looking at the
camera, everyone's smiling,

00:04:34.772 --> 00:04:37.023
everything's perfect, they
all have their makeup done.

00:04:37.023 --> 00:04:38.769
They look beautiful.

00:04:38.769 --> 00:04:42.553
When we try to take a family
photo, someone's always crying.

00:04:42.553 --> 00:04:43.527
Usually it's me.

00:04:43.527 --> 00:04:45.569
Someone's always not
looking at the camera.

00:04:45.569 --> 00:04:47.372
Someone's probably pooping.

00:04:47.372 --> 00:04:50.437
I just want that Neil Patrick Harris vibe

00:04:50.437 --> 00:04:52.355
coming from one of my pictures.

00:04:52.355 --> 00:04:54.418
It's like, we get it, Neil.

00:04:54.418 --> 00:04:55.295
You're perfect.

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:56.153
We get it.

00:04:56.153 --> 00:04:59.258
Can you just, like, post your
Halloween picture in November

00:04:59.258 --> 00:05:01.626
when the wound is a little less raw

00:05:01.626 --> 00:05:04.092
so that we feel a little
bit better about ourselves?

00:05:04.092 --> 00:05:06.869
And if you actually see this,
Neil Patrick Harris, thanks!

00:05:06.869 --> 00:05:08.268
Big fan of all your work.

00:05:08.268 --> 00:05:09.456
So that's all I got for today.

00:05:09.456 --> 00:05:11.486
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom,

00:05:11.486 --> 00:05:13.863
and if you guys know what
you're going to dress up as

00:05:13.863 --> 00:05:15.748
for Halloween, leave it in the comments,

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.611
'cause I desperately need ideas.

00:05:17.611 --> 00:05:20.479
And if you have couples
costume ideas, even better,

00:05:20.479 --> 00:05:23.518
because I wanna convince my
husband to dress up with me

00:05:23.518 --> 00:05:25.610
'cause we're coming for
you, Neil Patrick Harris.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:27.541
You and your perfect family,
we're coming for you,

00:05:27.541 --> 00:05:29.363
and we're going to take
a beautiful picture

00:05:29.363 --> 00:05:30.570
of all of us coordinated

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:33.035
with one random Kylo Ren in the corner.

00:05:33.035 --> 00:05:34.094
It's gonna look great.

00:05:34.094 --> 00:05:35.261
Til next time.

00:05:37.465 --> 00:05:38.298
I've always wanted to do that.

00:05:38.298 --> 00:05:40.494
Just, like, finish the
glass and just throw it down

00:05:40.494 --> 00:05:41.921
and walk away but this is my house

00:05:41.921 --> 00:05:45.482
and I don't want to have to clean it up.

00:05:45.482 --> 00:05:46.786
(Hannah sighs)

